BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Afro-Filipino Jazz Project
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T160000
DTSTAMP:20261025T114202Z
UID:dothebay-17207820@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:4
CATEGORIES:Outdoor & Recreation
DESCRIPTION:Free RSVP\n\nFew artists have appeared at the Festival more fr
 equently than flutist\, percussionist and arranger John Calloway. Whether 
 he’s leading his own band\, performing in the sextet of longtime creativ
 e partner John Santos\, or directing the Latin Jazz Youth Ensemble of San 
 Francisco\, Calloway is a Bay Area icon who’s been at the center of the 
 San Francisco Latin jazz scene for some five decades. But his latest and m
 ost personal project yet\, the Afro-Filipino Jazz Project\, takes his musi
 c in a new direction. Founded in 2022 as a creative\, interactive space\, 
 the Project is intended to bring together Afro Filipinx\, African American
  and Filipino American musicians to explore a broad range of musical style
 s\, with a particular emphasis on jazz idioms\, African American roots and
  traditional and folkloric Filipino music. It’s one component of the lar
 ger Afro-Filipino Project\, a platform dedicated to highlighting and celeb
 rating\, individually and collectively\, the art practices and artists of 
 the African American and Filipino American communities whose contributions
  have profoundly shaped our nation’s artistic narrative. For this perfor
 mance the AFJP features bass star Marcus Shelby\, inveterately grooving dr
 ummer Deszon Claiborne\, Latin jazz piano specialist Murray Low\, saxophon
 ist TJ Milan\, Conrad Benedicto on kulintang\, vocalist and dancer Ting Al
 varez and guest vocalist Anna Maria Flechero.\n\nFree RSVP\n\nDetails: htt
 ps://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/24/afro-filipino-jazz-project-tickets\nSo
 urce: DoTheBay\n\nAlso listed on:\n- https://sf.funcheap.com/silent-shorts
 -program/\n- https://sf.funcheap.com/free-bilingual-family-event-san-jos/
GEO:37.7850153;-122.4023464
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/31425269/5c59ff21-8070-4be0-8436-9d34d83bb6cf.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261025T114202Z
LOCATION:Yerba Buena Gardens covers two square city blocks bounded by Miss
 ion\, Folsom\, Third and Fourth Streets.\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94103
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/24/afro-filipino-jazz-project-tick
 ets
END:VEVENT
